#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:27
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:23
#. Diagram label
msgid "BA / Feature Requestor"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:67
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close issue ONLY on BA authorisation"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Computed, never chosen: `decisions/requirement-signoff-recorded.dmn` reads `signoffRecorded` and `signoffOutcome`, which `check:requirements` prints from the set's recorded sign-offs (its signoff-facts flag). `missing` loops back to the record; `proceed` is an approval (as written or amended); `stop` is a recorded reject, defer or cancel."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Confirm all criteria met"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:15
#. Diagram label
msgid "CRDM close-out"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:43
#. Diagram label
msgid "Feature sign-off on issue"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Holds no judgement in this diagram: both prior lanes already decided — sign-off, then confirmation against criteria — so this lane's only accountability is executing the close exactly when authorised and never before, on an issue that is the stakeholder's record rather than the agent's to close on its own reading of the thread."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:64
#. Diagram label
msgid "Land the feature's PRs"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:85
#. Diagram label
msgid "missing"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not accepted — recorded, with its reason"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Phase 6's \"explicit confirmation before merging to main\", made a step that can refuse. Once per pull request the feature still has open, after the sign-off is recorded and before the issue is closed: an issue is not closed on a feature that is not on `main`. `merge-to-main.bpmn` reads each head's evidence live, establishes that the owner authorised THAT merge (a stakeholder sign-off or the BA's confirmation is acceptance of the feature, not authorisation to merge it, unless the owner's own words say so), records the authorisation, merges, and confirms the base. A PR the owner holds or refuses stays open, and A_Close then waits: the BA's authorisation to close does not cover a feature that did not land. An increment the owner asked to land earlier in Phase 6 went through the same sub-process at that time. Where `cat-harness.sdlc` is switched on, this step is the opt-in process `merge-to-main` (`Process_MergeToMain`, sdlc/processes/merge-to-main.bpmn); it is not called from here, because a layer without that sub-graph does not have it (owner card Q-OPTIN-CALLS A, 2026-11-12)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Phase begins"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "Phase complete"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "proceed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reachable only through BA_Confirm, which is the BA saying every criterion is met. An agent must never close an issue without that explicit authorisation — the gate is the preceding task, and this name says so rather than leaving a reader to trace the flow for it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:55
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the sign-off attestation"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sign-off on the record?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stakeholders"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:45
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Stakeholders sign off on the delivered feature on the issue, having tested the built artefact rather than a description of it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Stands between stakeholder sign-off and the agent's close as an independent check against defined criteria — decision-audit, not a re-ask of the same yes/no the stakeholders already gave — and A_Close's own documentation says it is reachable ONLY through this confirmation, so the agent has no path to closing that bypasses it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:84
#. Diagram label
msgid "stop"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The business analyst confirms every acceptance criterion from the requirements is met. The issue closes only on their authorisation — an agent never closes an issue on its own say-so. It IS an adjudication with the requirement-set answers: an approval here moves the set to `accepted`, which `check:requirements` refuses unless it is a human's and every approved member is `in-force`."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The first of three sequential checks this diagram exists to enforce in order — sign off, confirm, close, never any other sequence — and what is being signed off here is the delivered FEATURE on the issue, not the requirement model that crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn's Lane_Stakeholders approved earlier in the process."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The stakeholders sign off, the BA confirms every criterion is met, the feature lands on `main` through the `merge-to-main` sub-process, and only then does the agent close the issue. Never the other way round: an agent must never assume completion."
msgstr ""
